Changes: `relayvsr/wan.py`, `relayvsr/flash.py` and `relayvsr/kernels.py` re-implement the
streaming inference path of `refvsr_inference/models/wan/{transformer,lq_proj,spatial_attention}.py`,
`refvsr_inference/models/flash/{model,_flashvsr_ops,_local_attention,_local_attention_triton}.py`
and `refvsr_inference/runtime/streaming.py` with the checkpoints' module names: training, block-causal
and FlexAttention paths, gradient checkpointing, Diffusers mixins and checkpoint loading are removed;
the one-step flow-matching update is written out (t=1000, sigma 1 to 0); the timestep and text
conditioning are recomputed per keyframe instead of cached; keyframe K/V are held by the Runtime's
memory; RoPE tables are built per call instead of held as buffers. Both Triton kernels take shapes,
strides and windows as arguments instead of compile-time constants, and the Flash kernel serves only
its forward with no plane mask or relative RoPE. Masked SDPA over row bands replaces upstream's
reference paths. Noise comes from the request's CPU generator. Output frames are rounded from F32
rather than truncated from bf16, and are area-scaled to the requested size.
